## Why This Is Asked
To test understanding of runtime extensibility and decoupled design. This beginner-level question focuses on registries and the strategy pattern rather than hardcoding flags.

## Key Concepts
- Strategy pattern for pluggable evaluation logic
- Registry pattern for runtime extensibility
- Context-aware evaluation with user attributes

## Code Example
```typescript
interface Context { userId: number; segment?: string; }
type Strategy = (ctx: Context, feature: string) => boolean;

class Registry {
  private map = new Map<string, () => Strategy>();

  register(name: string, factory: () => Strategy) {
    this.map.set(name, factory);
  }

  get(name: string): Strategy | undefined {
    return this.map.get(name)?.();
  }
}

class FeatureEngine {
  constructor(private registry: Registry) {}

  isEnabled(feature: string, ctx: Context): boolean {
    const strategy = this.registry.get(feature);
    return strategy ? strategy(ctx, feature) : false;
  }
}

// Usage: Add percent strategy at runtime
const registry = new Registry();
registry.register('percent', () => 
  (ctx, feature) => Math.abs(hash(ctx.userId + feature)) % 100 < 50
);

const engine = new FeatureEngine(registry);
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design an extensible plugin mechanism using simple interfaces and a runtime registry.

## Key Concepts

- Registry pattern for dynamic extension
- Conflict resolution via priority or timestamp
- Preconditions gating and graceful fallbacks

## Code Example

```ts
interface Command {
  id: string
  name: string
  prerequisites?: string[]
  execute(ctx: any): void
}

class Registry {
  private map = new Map<string, {cmd: Command, priority: number, ts: number}>();
  register(cmd: Command, priority = 0){
    this.map.set(cmd.name, {cmd, priority, ts: Date.now()});
  }
  dispatch(name: string, ctx: any){
    const entry = this.map.get(name);
    if(!entry) return;
    if((entry.cmd.prerequisites ?? []).some(p => !ctx.flags?.includes(p))) return;
    entry.cmd.execute(ctx);
  }
  unregister(name: string){ this.map.delete(name); }
  clear(){ this.map.clear(); }
}
``` 

